purpose: The box tree and its geometry. Turns a styled document into positioned boxes.

allow: util dom html css gfx

public: Box.h FloatContext.h FontTextMeasurer.h LayoutEngine.h

extern:

max_tu_lines: 900

budget: BoxGeometry     header_lines=30 public_methods=6  members=4
# Fragments are the seventh member. A wrapped text box occupies one rectangle
# per line and there is nowhere else to put them; a single geometry meant the
# last line overwrote every earlier one.
# One more member and two more methods for `background-image`: a box may carry
# both a content image and a background one, they paint at different times, and
# a single slot would make a replaced element with a background lose one of them.
# One more member and two more methods for the intrinsic width cache. It is a
# cache rather than a computation because sizing a table's columns measures
# every cell's subtree, and a nested table did that once per ancestor -- 70% of
# the time to lay out a comment page, growing with nesting depth.
# Three more methods for positioning: the question "is this box out of the
# flow entirely", and mutable access to the children and fragments. The two
# mutable accessors are what the second pass needs -- a relative offset and an
# absolute placement both move a subtree that already has geometry, and
# geometry is absolute, so a box that moves takes everything under it.
# Raised for `display: inline-block`. Two methods and a kind: IsAtomicInline,
# which every pass that distinguishes "walked through" from "placed as a
# rectangle" has to ask, and ClipsOverflow, which moved here from
# css::ComputedStyle because `overflow` does not apply to a non-replaced inline
# box and only the box knows whether it is one. Asking the style instead
# deleted every story title on old.reddit.com.
budget: Box             header_lines=175 public_methods=41 members=10
# The kinds are documented rather than listed, because each one exists to make
# a distinction some pass would otherwise have to rediscover from style. The
# budget is here so that growth in the vocabulary is a decision.
budget: Kind            header_lines=40 public_methods=0 members=0
budget: ImageProvider   header_lines=25 public_methods=6  members=0
budget: TextFragment    header_lines=25 public_methods=4  members=4
budget: TextMeasurer    header_lines=30 public_methods=8  members=0
budget: FontTextMeasurer header_lines=35 public_methods=8 members=1
# Raised for the two intrinsic-width entry points and their measurement pair.
# The split is the point: the cached form is what the recursion must call, and
# a comment on one function cannot say that -- measuring through the wrong one
# reintroduces an O(nodes x nesting depth) walk that was 70% of the time to lay
# out a comment page.
budget: LayoutEngine    header_lines=95 public_methods=8  members=3
# The floats in one block formatting context. Separate from Box because it
# belongs to the context rather than to any box in it: a float shortens line
# boxes that belong to boxes which know nothing about it.
budget: FloatContext    header_lines=70 public_methods=14 members=1
